2. Git Conflict: 
A merge conflict in Git happens when changes in two branches affect the same part of a file and Git cannot automatically merge them. 
To handle it, I first identify the conflicted files using Git’s markers, then manually resolve the conflict by choosing or combining the changes. 
After resolving, I run git add to mark the files as resolved and commit the merge. This ensures the code is correctly 
combined without losing any important changes.


